{
 "turns_text": [
  "[SEG0001] person_1 (CLINICAL_STAFF): sorry, we're running a bit behind this arvo. uh, your partner rang the front desk, said you'd had a bit of a turn.",
  "[SEG0002] person_2 (PATIENT): yeah, sorry I'm late too. the tram was a nightmare and I nearly just went home.",
  "[SEG0003] person_3 (DOCTOR): you're here. what happened.",
  "[SEG0004] person_2 (PATIENT): I thought I was having a heart attack. on the train.",
  "[SEG0005] person_2 (PATIENT): my chest went all tight out of nowhere, and I started shaking, and I got really scared. I'm only twenty-three. is that actually a heart attack?",
  "[SEG0006] person_3 (DOCTOR): when did it start.",
  "[SEG0007] person_2 (PATIENT): yesterday morning. umm, I was on the city loop, just standing there, and it hit me.",
  "[SEG0008] person_3 (DOCTOR): tight now.",
  "[SEG0009] person_2 (PATIENT): no. it's gone. it lasted twenty minutes... no, ten minutes.",
  "[SEG0010] person_3 (DOCTOR): and the shaking.",
  "[SEG0011] person_2 (PATIENT): yeah, the shaking stopped. but I'm still really scared it's my heart. what if it happens on the train tomorrow?",
  "[SEG0012] person_3 (DOCTOR): any pain in the arm or the jaw.",
  "[SEG0013] person_2 (PATIENT): no. no arm pain, no jaw pain.",
  "[SEG0014] person_3 (DOCTOR): short of breath.",
  "[SEG0015] person_2 (PATIENT): during it, yeah, I couldn't get a proper breath. not now. is that dangerous?",
  "[SEG0016] person_3 (DOCTOR): any sweats.",
  "[SEG0017] person_2 (PATIENT): no. no sweats.",
  "[SEG0018] person_3 (DOCTOR): ever happened before.",
  "[SEG0019] person_2 (PATIENT): never. first time ever. my partner reckoned I should've gone to emergency. should I have?",
  "[SEG0020] person_3 (DOCTOR): right. any heart disease in the family.",
  "[SEG0021] person_2 (PATIENT): my dad had a stent put in. last year... or maybe the year before, I get mixed up. he's on asprin now. does that mean I'll get one too?",
  "[SEG0022] person_3 (DOCTOR): not on its own. do you smoke.",
  "[SEG0023] person_2 (PATIENT): no. never smoked. I'll have a beer on the weekend sometimes, that's it.",
  "[SEG0024] person_3 (DOCTOR): any tablets. any drugs.",
  "[SEG0025] person_2 (PATIENT): no drugs. nah, no tablets, nothing.",
  "[SEG0026] person_3 (DOCTOR): allergies.",
  "[SEG0027] person_2 (PATIENT): no. no allergies.",
  "[SEG0028] person_1 (CLINICAL_STAFF): obs are in. blood pressure is one oh nine over seventy-seven. temperature thirty-eight point three.",
  "[SEG0029] person_1 (CLINICAL_STAFF): heart rate one hundred and four. oxygen sats ninety-nine percent. weight, last time in March you were sixty-eight, today fifty-four... no, fifty-two kilos. your last pressure was one-forty.",
  "[SEG0030] person_3 (DOCTOR): chest is clear. heart sounds normal, just a bit quick. any cough.",
  "[SEG0031] person_2 (PATIENT): no cough. I'm alright otherwise, just scared. will the heart trace hurt? do I have to stop getting the train?",
  "[SEG0032] person_3 (DOCTOR): the ECG won't hurt and I'll get one done today. most likely a panic attack. I can't exclude a rhythm problem until the tracing's back.",
  "[SEG0033] person_3 (DOCTOR): if the tightness hasn't settled we might organise a chest x-ray. I'm not booking that now.",
  "[SEG0034] person_3 (DOCTOR): when it starts, breathe in for four and out for six. I'll see you in two weeks. call an ambulance if you get crushing pain or you collapse."
 ],
